			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
			)
		)
		(property "Description" "GENERIC eMMC 5.1 (JESD84-B51), 153-ball FBGA, 11.5x13mm body, 0.5mm pitch, JEDEC MO-276-class outline. Part-agnostic land verified across THREE independent sources that agree ball-for-ball: (1) Kingston EMMC08G-ML36-01B00 datasheet v1.9 (Table 9 Ball Assignment); (2) Alliance Memory 64/128/256/512GB eMMC datasheet Rev.1.0 (Table 4 Pin List, exact text); (3) Zetta ZDEMMC08GA real manufacturer EasyEDA/LCSC symbol+footprint (LCSC C3029818) pulled via easyeda2kicad and cross-checked pin-for-pin -- all three agree on the JEDEC-standard signal ball set (CLK M6, CMD M5, DAT0-2 A3-A5, DAT3-7 B2-B6, RST_n K5, DS/RCLK H5, VCC x4 E6/F5/J10/K9, VCCQ x5 C6/M4/N4/P3/P5, VSS x6 A6/E7/G5/H10/J5/K8, VSSQ x5 C4/N2/N5/P4/P6, VDDi C2) and on the exact 153-position depopulated ball pattern (cross-validated row-by-row). The remaining ~120 balls are RFU/VSF/NC per all sources -- vendor-specific by definition (Kingston/Zetta mark some as RFU or VSF, Alliance repurposes P7 as a vendor debug UART TX -- NOT part of the generic JEDEC set, left as NC here). MPN is density/vendor-specific and TBD (RFQ pending, see hub-ent-bom-detailed.md open item 6) -- this symbol/footprint is the reusable land, not a specific orderable part."
			(at 0 0 0)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(hide yes)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
			)
		)
		(property "Manufacturer" "Generic / part-agnostic (JEDEC eMMC 5.1, JESD84-B51)"
